    "text": "A disc of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>kg</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is rotating with an angular velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>rad</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, about an axis passing through its centre and perpendicular to its plane. If a mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.25</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>kg</mi></math> is stuck on the periphery of the disc, then its angular velocity will become",
